      "amount": "1 packet",
      "notes": "optional for fermentation"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Roast the beef bones in the oven for 30 minutes.",
    "In a large pot, sauté the chopped onion and sliced ginger in a little water until softened.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the roasted beef bones, fish sauce, soy sauce, brown sugar, and black pepper to the pot.",
    "Pour in the water and bring the mixture to a boil.",
    "Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 2 hours.",
    "Strain the broth through a fine-mesh sieve into a clean pot.",
    "Add the rice vinegar and optional salt to the broth.",
    "If desired, add a fermentation starter and let the broth ferment at room temperature for 1-3 days.",
    "Strain the broth again before serving.",
    "Serve hot with noodles or rice."
  ],
